  "discussion": "A medium period swell out of the north-northwest (325 to 350 degree) will hold through the rest of the afternoon before gradually decreasing tonight. Another small to moderate swell fills in Monday night, keeping small to moderate surf in place through Tuesday. A large northwest to north- northwest swell is then forecast to arrive late Wednesday into Thursday and could bring surf near or right at warning levels. A small south-southwest swell will keep seasonal average surf in place this afternoon before declining Monday through the remainder of the week. Rough surf along east-facing shores will hold at or above seasonal average tonight and tomorrow. Surf will decrease slightly by Tuesday as trades begin to ease before increasing again by Wednesday.",
